{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_bohfly4o6c4jxxwctbt5yno7ya2s23nxnux6wcvalhudxesrmnxq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01QhMe8R4cMkur8jdUpDXijg","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ihIbAd/translation/ERRORS.md","content":"# ERRORS.md — Phase A: error / rejection surface table\n\nMechanically derived from `c_src/src/lib.c`. Every `return` that is guarded by a\nvalidity check, every early-out / `continue`, every explicit range check, every\nnull check, every min/max constant, and every implicit truncation bound is one\nrow. There are **no** `assert`s, no error enums, no `RETURN_ERROR` macros and no\n`errno` usage in this library (`grep -c 'assert\\|errno\\|RETURN_ERROR' → 0`), so\nrejections are expressed purely as sentinel return values (`-1`, `0`) and as\n`continue` skips.\n\n## Notes on reachability\n\n`memchra2` is the **only** dynamically exported symbol (see `SYMBOLS.md`). All\nguarded helpers are `static` and are called by `memchra2` with hard-coded,\nalways-valid arguments (stack arrays, string literals, constant counts). A row\nis therefore annotated:\n\n* **R** = reachable by varying `a`/`b`/`c`/`d` through the FFI boundary →\n  a differential test drives the exact condition through `memchra2`.\n* **U** = statically unreachable from the public API. The C compiler still emits\n  (or folds) the check; the Rust translation must contain the *same* check with\n  the *same* sentinel so that behaviour is identical for the reachable path and\n  the code is a faithful translation. Verified by (a) code inspection of the\n  guard + sentinel, and (b) a differential test that pins the *observable*\n  consequence of the branch that IS taken (the `else` side), so any change to the\n  guard would change `memchra2`'s output and be caught.\n\n## Table\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | reach